From d0b937a64a9576cb1eb14829419208f375ad0027 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bigoovip <86590318+bigoovip@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 15:23:19 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] caldav: export DUE/DTSTART/DTEND with TZID + VTIMEZONE,
 keep timestamps in UTC

Downstream patch: iOS Reminders showed server-sent reminders as GMT because the
CalDAV export wrote bare UTC with no TZID/VTIMEZONE. Wall-clock fields (DUE,
DTSTART, DTEND, RRULE BYMONTHDAY) are now rendered in the CalDAV user's timezone
with a TZID plus a matching VTIMEZONE block; DTSTAMP, CREATED, COMPLETED,
LAST-MODIFIED and VALARM TRIGGER stay UTC per RFC 5545.
GetCaldavTodosForTasks takes the timezone as a third argument.
